# Pulse contribution typecheck - the confidence check, runnable in the sandbox without node_modules

Generated 2026-09-02 05:53 UTC. Repo tip before this commit: ff562511.
A full fork build is impossible here (desktop/vscode/node_modules is empty), but the workbench's own
strict compiler flags can still be pointed at Pulse's contribution alone: the sources it imports are
all in-tree, so only third-party @types are missing, and those surface as errors in *other* people's
files, never in ours.

    cd desktop/vscode/src
    node ../../../pulse-webview/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc -p tsconfig.pulseai-check.json

TypeScript 6.0.3 (resolved from pulse-webview/node_modules, which the repo already installs).
Config src/tsconfig.pulseai-check.json: extends src/tsconfig.base.json (strict, noUnusedLocals,
noImplicitOverride, noImplicitReturns, moduleResolution nodenext), noEmit, types:[], include =
src/typings/**/*.d.ts + contrib/pulseai/{browser,common}. node/ and electron-browser/ are out of scope
because they need @types/node and electron.d.ts from a real install; the full build still checks them.

## First run: what it caught in code this branch already shipped

Six real defects in browser/, all invisible to a transpile-only check, all fixed in this commit. The TS2882 css-import errors and every TS2591 in
node/ are config-scope artifacts (src/typings declares *.css; node needs @types/node), so they are
listed out rather than fixed.

    vs/workbench/contrib/pulseai/browser/pulseAIIcons.ts(65,2): error TS2740: Type 'SVGSVGElement' is missing the following properties from type 'HTMLElement': accessKey, accessKeyLabel, autocapitalize, autocorrect, and 26 more.
    vs/workbench/contrib/pulseai/browser/pulseAIRenderer.ts(10,25): error TS6133: 'isSilentTool' is declared but its value is never read.
    vs/workbench/contrib/pulseai/browser/pulseAIRenderer.ts(530,14): error TS6133: 'index' is declared but its value is never read.
    vs/workbench/contrib/pulseai/browser/pulseAIViewPane.ts(26,2): error TS2741: Property 'align' is missing in type 'HTMLElement' but required in type 'HTMLParagraphElement'.
    vs/workbench/contrib/pulseai/browser/pulseAIViewPane.ts(135,3): error TS2740: Type 'HTMLElement' is missing the following properties from type 'HTMLIFrameElement': align, allow, allowFullscreen, contentDocument, and 15 more.
    vs/workbench/contrib/pulseai/browser/pulseAIViewPane.ts(151,32): error TS2345: Argument of type 'HTMLElement' is not assignable to parameter of type 'HTMLIFrameElement'.

Raw pulseai lines in that run: 26; the 6 above are the ones in this lane.

